  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1214 AM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nThe ridge currently centered over the southwestern CONUS will re-\ncenter over our area by Sunday, and then eventually the southeastern \nU. S. by Monday. Although the center of the ridge will not be on top \nof us through the rest of next week, the ridge will be expansive and \nstill be the main influence over our weather. What that means for \nwest-central Texas is continued warmer than normal temperatures in \nthe upper 90s to around 103 on Sunday, then a very slow cooling of \nhighs into the mid and upper 90s by the end of next week. Normal \nhighs now through late next week range from around 88 to 90 degrees. \nNo significant chance of precipitation is expected until next Friday.",
